{#
  Site-wide notice, rendered as a bold gig-poster billboard at the top of the
  page content. Data lives in site.json under `notice`:

    active    — master on/off switch (see base.njk)
    label     — short kicker, e.g. "Fringe 2026"
    message   — the sentence shown to visitors (doubles as the headline)
    linkText  — call-to-action text (optional)
    linkUrl   — root-absolute link, run through `rel` (optional)

  Deliberately not dismissible: the notice carries critical information (e.g.
  the Wednesday sessions being off), so every visit should see it. Reusable for
  the annual Fringe pause, venue moves, one-off events, etc. Flip `active` to
  switch it on and off.
#}
{% set n = site.notice %}
<aside class="notice-poster" aria-label="Site notice">
  {% if n.label %}<p class="notice-poster__kicker">&#9733;&ensp;{{ n.label }}&ensp;&#9733;</p>{% endif %}
  <p class="notice-poster__msg">{{ n.message }}</p>
  {% if n.linkText and n.linkUrl %}<a class="btn btn--primary notice-poster__cta" href="{{ n.linkUrl | rel }}">{{ n.linkText }} &rarr;</a>{% endif %}
</aside>
